  "reasoning": "The input molecule is a pinacol boronate ester of a phenyl ring substituted with a cyclopropanecarboxamide group. The reaction type is Functional Group Interconversion (FGI). In retrosynthetic analysis, the standard FGI for a pinacol boronate ester is its hydrolysis to the corresponding boronic acid. Disconnection of the cyclic boronate ester linkage at the boron-oxygen bonds and replacement of the pinacol diol moiety with hydroxyl groups yields the boronic acid precursor. The forward reaction corresponds to the hydrolysis of the boronate ester to form the boronic acid and pinacol.",
  "final_answer": "O=C(c1ccc(B(O)O)cc1)NC1CC1"
}

